; Records asked for. First a card T; then for each card two out: the number of the table record it asks for, its
; last two digits when it is T or more (a number word is 700 + its record in the numbers deck, a spelled letter 100
; or 200 + its code), else 0, and the card itself. The host fetches the record and deals it after the card to the
; machine that needs it (numf, names).
;
; Address Contents Label Opcode Operand Comment
  03                    INP   t        03-03: T
  04            rec     INP   c        04-15: a card
  05                    CLA   c
  06                    SUB   t
  07                    TAC   no
  08                    CLA   c
  09                    SFT   22
  10                    STO   r
  11                    JMP   put
  12            no      CLA   z
  13                    STO   r
  14            put     OUT   r
  15                    OUT   c
  16                    JMP   rec
  20            t       DATA  0
  21            c       DATA  0
  22            r       DATA  0
  23            z       DATA  0
